# Keep the Docker build context lean — these are rebuilt inside the image or
# are host-only artifacts. Sending them bloats the context and fills the VM disk.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/dist
**/build
**/.gradle
**/.dart_tool
packages/sdk-flutter/example/build
packages/sdk-android/**/build
packages/rulemind-core-rs/target
packages/rulemind-core-rs/pkg
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.runtime
**/.runtime

# `.venv` alone did NOT match this repo's actual virtualenv, which is
# `.venv-rulemind` (~511MB). Both images build with `context: .`, so that whole
# tree was tarred and shipped to the Docker daemon on every single build.
.venv
.venv*
**/.venv
**/.venv*
venv
**/venv

# SECRETS. apps/web/Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and a real `.env` with live
# credentials exists at the repo root — it was being baked into the web image,
# which then gets pushed to a registry. `.env.example` is deliberately kept.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

**/coverage
